{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1390094-american-mantels-a-suggestion","id":1390094,"title":"American Mantels (a suggestion)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-19T16:46:21-07:00","id":1390094,"title":"American Mantels (a suggestion)","content":"This thread is based on my recent purchase and pleasure in reading &quot;Mantels of Washington.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, which Americans real, fictional, or folkloric, have generated mantels? <br /> <br /> Note: Native Americans who became famous since the founding of the USA are eligible. Sitting Bull, Geronimo, Sacagawea, Crazy Horse, Pocahontas, and Squanto, might all have mantels. However, Native Americans who are only famous to other Native Americans would have mantels only within a Native American tradition.<br /> <br /> So, who would you put in the list?<br /> <br /> Abraham Lincoln, Benjamin Franklin, Thomas Jefferson, and Tom Paine, stike me as automatic inclusions. Teddy Roosevelt, FDR, and Elenore Roosevelt, seem highly likely. Dr. King, Malcolm X, Susan B. Anthony, and Mother Jones, seem like good bets.<br /> <br /> Outlaws like Al Capone, Bonny and Clyde, Blackbeard, Quantrel, Jesse James, would provide dark and sinister mantels.<br /> <br /> A small number of celebrities who's celebrity has lasted long enough like Chaplin, Bettie Davis, John Wayne, James Dean, Elvis or Joplin, might have mantels too. It would be a matter of how long and intense their celebrity was. Lilian Gish was famous for decades, but never that famous. Others were more famous that Elvis, for a few years and long outlived their fame.<br /> <br /> Which folkloric figures get mantels would involve how important their story is. John Henry was deeply important to many different communities. I read of a Klu Kluxer that loudly and publicly protested John Henry's song and story being removed from the school curriculum because &quot;John Henry was the noblest hero of the American Working Man.&quot; There are Black Panther party members that would agree with him.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Pecos Bill was fakelore for children from day one. These days he's only known by the Disney cartoons. Meanwhile, both Bugs Bunny and Mickey Mouse have both been world famous and deeply loved for decades.<br /> <br /> So, who are the American Mantels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-20-2020, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T00:33:43-07:00","id":1390217,"title":"","content":"I have a question. Why limit yourself to American Mantles? There are plenty of individuals across the world that might be eligible to have generated Mantles.<br /> Also, Eliot Ness. Feels like he's another person who would generate a Mantle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T01:22:03-07:00","id":1390222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1390094-american-mantels-a-suggestion?p=1390217#post1390217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question. Why limit yourself to American Mantles? There are plenty of individuals across the world that might be eligible to have generated Mantles.<br /> Also, Eliot Ness. Feels like he's another person who would generate a Mantle.</div> </div> </div> </div>They specifically started a thread asking about Americans, so that's what we're doing. A conversation talking about other cultures' mantels can be its own thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T01:32:30-07:00","id":1390224,"title":"","content":"Bass Fukkin Reeves.<br /> <br /> The most successful Lawman in the West, having brought in over 3000 criminals in his time as a Deputy U.S. Marshal, while only ever having killed 14, and only in self defense.<br /> <br /> Many believe that he was a primary inspiration for the Lone Ranger.<br /> <br /> And a smaller but still very important qualification: <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BassReeves.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">His mustache alone is worth at least one Legend</a><br /> <br /> Now, admittedly, a slight problem with this topic is that to be frank I don't think a lot of US folklore, tall tale, or similar figures got past Hero. Most of them don't seem to reach beyond the scope of what Scion presumes Heroes can do, with only a very few reaching to Demigod.<br /> <br /> And this may be the &quot;I remember the 1E Yankee Pantheon&quot; speaking but it'd be a hard sell to convince me any of them are Godly.<br /> <br /> So yeah. I can see some figures like John Henry or Bass Reeves being Heroes, maybe Demigods, but I dunno if i'd say that they're Gods. Pablo's Mantles of Washington managed to make a good case for Washington, but it'll be tough for me to easily buy others.<br /> <br /> And that's okay, TBH. You don't need to be a God-tier cosmic force to have made an impact in Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-22-2020, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T08:10:40-07:00","id":1390973,"title":"","content":"Yeah Bass Reeves looks pretty bad ass. Definitely a hero scion with a high legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}